frontend/src/methodology.md:41:It's possible that MPs make mistakes when entering declaration records. Company numbers may be incorrect or address may differ slightly. We had to decide whether to take a strict or lax approach to aggregating companies with malformed data. We opted for a relaxed approach. This means that we match on similar addresses and ignore conflicting IDs if there is an address match. A more relaxed approach means there are more cohesive groupings of funders. We think this makes analysis easier. With stricter rules, search queries like 'BBC' or 'Google' may return several of individual donors which is non-sensical.
frontend/src/methodology.md:54:Parliamentary data is available under the [Open Parliament Licence v3.0](https://www.parliament.uk/site-information/copyright-parliament/open-parliament-licence/). When reusing it, include the required attribution:
